HEAD


To complete this level, let's detach HEAD from bugFix and attach it to the commit instead.
Specify this commit by its hash. The hash for each commit is displayed on the circle that represents the commit.

git checkout bugFix^——>by using ref

HEAD normally current branch ko point karta hai, aur current branch latest commit ko point karti hai.
So technically chain hoti hai:

HEAD → branch → commit


Aur jab detached ho:

A --- B --- C
      ↑
     HEAD

main ───────→ C
Ab HEAD branch ko point nahi karta, directly commit ko point karta hai.









Bas ek important correction hai:
HEAD hamesha branch ko target nahi karta. Normal state mein HEAD → branch → commit hota hai. But detached HEAD mein HEAD → commit directly hota hai.
Normal situation

A → B → C
        ↑
      bugFix
        ↑
       HEAD

Yahan:

git checkout HEAD^

aur

git checkout bugFix^

same commit par le jayenge, because:

HEAD → bugFix → C

So:

HEAD^    = C ka parent = B
bugFix^  = C ka parent = B

✅ Same.

But yahan difference aa jata hai 👇
Suppose:

A → B → C
        ↑
      bugFix

A → B → C → D
            ↑
           main
            ↑
           HEAD

Ab:

HEAD → main → D
bugFix → C

Therefore:

git checkout HEAD^

➡️ D ka parent = C
while:

git checkout bugFix^

➡️ C ka parent = B
So:

HEAD^     → C
bugFix^   → B

And detached HEAD ke baad aur clear ho jayega

A → B → C
        ↑
      bugFix

       HEAD
        ↓
        B

Ab HEAD branch ko point nahi kar raha.
If you do:

git checkout HEAD^

➡️ A
But:

git checkout bugFix^

➡️ B
Because HEAD aur bugFix alag commits par hain.
